# <%= projectName %>

Go walking skeleton scaffolded by keel — hexagonal, one module, no
mediator object: commands are structs, driving ports are per-use-case
interfaces, and each `cmd/` main is the assembly point.

## Layout

```
cmd/            — one directory per deployment unit; each main.go
                  wires the hexagon by hand (constructor injection)
internal/
  domain/       — the contract face: commands, ports, and the
                  exported factories returning driving ports
    internal/   — the compiler-hidden core: entities and domain
                  services, unimportable from outside the domain
                  subtree
  app/          — primary adapters: transport → command → port →
                  transport; zero business logic
  infra/        — secondary adapters, one directory per technology;
                  each port's canonical fake lives here too
```

Cross-cutting concerns (logging, metrics, tx) wrap the driving ports
as decorator functions applied at the assembly point.

## Test

```sh
go test ./...
```

## Deployment units

Each `cmd/` directory is one deployment unit; its `main.go` import
list reads like the ops runbook.
